WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.053
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:10.323 --> 00:12.784
We don't know who the requester is either.

3
00:12.867 --> 00:14.452
-Honestly! -You little bastard.

4
00:14.536 --> 00:16.830
I'm sorry, sir! I was wrong.

5
00:16.913 --> 00:20.542
I promise I won't do it again. I'll be good and listen to my parents.

6
00:20.625 --> 00:21.918
That's a given, punk.

7
00:22.001 --> 00:23.878
I don't know anything about this.

8
00:23.962 --> 00:26.464
If someone pays, we post whatever they want online.

9
00:26.548 --> 00:28.842
Repost it and generate some traffic--

10
00:28.925 --> 00:31.511
That's called manipulating public opinion, punk.

11
00:32.011 --> 00:34.806
No wonder they're setting up a cyber investigation unit.

12
00:34.889 --> 00:36.349
Hey, your name.

13
00:36.850 --> 00:38.434
Your name. Now.

14
00:42.397 --> 00:43.898
It's a bust.

15
00:45.108 --> 00:46.943
Where did you learn that word?

16
00:47.026 --> 00:49.487
It comes up often in Korean dramas.

17
00:52.574 --> 00:53.616
Stand up.

18
00:55.326 --> 00:57.871
-Hello, ma'am. -Hello, ma'am.

19
00:58.955 --> 01:01.291
You motherfuckers and your cigarettes.

20
01:05.628 --> 01:09.090
You arrested a bunch of paid commenters instead of a serial killer?

21
01:09.591 --> 01:11.092
Who took the lead on this?

22
01:11.176 --> 01:12.218
Apologies, ma'am.

23
01:13.178 --> 01:14.679
Stay put. Just keep quiet.

24
01:14.762 --> 01:17.307
Save your apology for your parents who brought you into this world.

25
01:17.390 --> 01:20.643
Apologize for growing up with fuck-all going on up there,

26
01:20.727 --> 01:21.686
you shit-for-brains.

27
01:21.769 --> 01:24.272
Seriously, why do you even live? Why bother?

28
01:24.355 --> 01:25.231
A real…

29
01:25.315 --> 01:26.316
Shit-for-brains?

30
01:26.399 --> 01:27.358
Yes.

31
01:31.237 --> 01:33.823
The Japanese gent is here too.

32
01:38.453 --> 01:39.829
It's a pleasure to meet you.

33
01:40.413 --> 01:42.415
I'm head of the Mobile Investigation Unit.

34
01:43.041 --> 01:44.250
Nice to meet you.

35
01:44.834 --> 01:46.711
This must have been so hard on you.

36
01:46.794 --> 01:48.588
Thanks to these half-wits,

37
01:48.671 --> 01:51.049
you're going through so much in a foreign country.

38
01:54.177 --> 01:55.011
She says you're--

39
01:55.094 --> 01:56.221
It's no problem.

40
01:57.597 --> 02:00.099
Anyway, please let your bosses know

41
02:00.183 --> 02:02.852
that everything's fine here and that the Korean police

42
02:03.353 --> 02:05.772
are so very competent.

43
02:06.564 --> 02:08.816
Yes, of course. I will.

44
02:13.696 --> 02:15.365
What a fucking embarrassment.

45
02:15.448 --> 02:16.324
What was that?

46
02:17.158 --> 02:18.034
What did she say?

47
02:18.534 --> 02:21.037
If you fail one more time…

48
02:22.789 --> 02:24.165
that's it for this unit.

49
02:24.249 --> 02:25.959
-Yes, ma'am! -Yes, ma'am!

50
02:27.293 --> 02:29.212
Useless fucks.

51
02:31.631 --> 02:32.757
Ma'am…

52
02:37.136 --> 02:38.554
She's so badass.

53
02:45.937 --> 02:48.606
There's something about that kid.

54
02:51.025 --> 02:51.943
Like what?

55
02:53.027 --> 02:54.279
-Get in. -Move it.

56
02:54.362 --> 02:55.196
Get in.

57
02:55.280 --> 02:56.406
You. Come here.

58
02:56.906 --> 02:58.950
Let's have a quick chat. Wait here.

59
02:59.033 --> 03:00.159
-Understood, sir. -Sorry?

60
03:00.243 --> 03:01.536
-Come here. -Why…

61
03:02.412 --> 03:03.288
You…

62
03:03.913 --> 03:05.873
Do you have any idea how scary prison is?

63
03:06.666 --> 03:07.834
Stand here.

64
03:09.127 --> 03:11.129
Why are you doing this?

65
03:11.713 --> 03:14.257
You know something, don't you?

66
03:14.340 --> 03:15.216
Sorry?

67
03:15.300 --> 03:17.135
If you talk to us now,

68
03:17.635 --> 03:20.430
you could just do detention, not prison time.

69
03:23.224 --> 03:24.058
Really?

70
03:24.142 --> 03:26.811
-Yes. -Depends on what you tell us.

71
03:28.563 --> 03:29.439
So?

72
03:33.776 --> 03:34.944
Good luck inside, then.

73
03:36.529 --> 03:37.447
Wait, sir.

74
03:37.530 --> 03:38.698
Yeah?

75
03:38.781 --> 03:39.949
That post…

76
03:40.450 --> 03:41.284
The post?

77
03:45.455 --> 03:49.334
I checked out the account of the person who requested it.

78
03:53.379 --> 03:56.299
The post they requested about the Imjin War and stuff

79
03:56.841 --> 03:57.925
was a bit unusual.

80
03:59.010 --> 04:02.013
"The Imjin War"?

81
04:02.513 --> 04:04.599
What the hell's this bastard's deal?

82
04:05.641 --> 04:09.270
I thought it might be a prank, so I checked out the requester's account.

83
04:12.815 --> 04:13.775
"Emi"?

84
04:17.695 --> 04:19.989
THIS ACCOUNT HAS BEEN DELETED

85
04:20.073 --> 04:22.158
It definitely said "Emi"…

86
04:22.658 --> 04:24.243
No, "E-M-I"!

87
04:24.744 --> 04:27.163
I think that account's been deleted, though…

88
04:31.000 --> 04:35.088
So you're saying the user ID of the person who requested the post about Emiri…

89
04:37.465 --> 04:38.966
was Emi, is that it?

90
04:39.550 --> 04:40.510
That's right.

91
04:41.844 --> 04:43.513
Thanks for the valuable info.

92
04:43.596 --> 04:45.431
There goes your reduced sentence.

93
04:45.515 --> 04:47.600
-Get him on the bus. -Yes, sir.

94
04:47.683 --> 04:49.602
-You can go. -Go where?

95
04:49.685 --> 04:50.520
-Sir? -Come here.

96
04:50.603 --> 04:52.105
-You said you'd help. -Come here.

97
04:52.188 --> 04:53.022
Easy.

98
04:53.106 --> 04:54.732
Hey, wait!

99
04:54.816 --> 04:57.151
-Zip it, you little shit. -That hurts!

100
04:57.777 --> 05:00.530
YANGHWA SUPERMARKET

101
05:04.867 --> 05:06.160
Thanks. Have a good night.

102
05:30.977 --> 05:32.395
Hogging it all by yourself?

103
05:33.354 --> 05:34.522
Unbelievable.

104
05:38.693 --> 05:42.029
Be honest. You don't have any friends, do you?

105
05:47.160 --> 05:50.913
The police academy's golden boy. A self-centered bachelor.

106
05:52.623 --> 05:54.834
Bet you still live with your mom, don't you?

107
05:59.338 --> 06:00.548
This bastard…

108
06:03.468 --> 06:06.220
He's sharper than I thought.

109
06:08.556 --> 06:10.850
He seems to know quite a bit about us too.

110
06:13.269 --> 06:15.480
He was testing when the cops would take the bait.

111
06:16.272 --> 06:18.399
Now he'll move even more carefully.

112
06:23.905 --> 06:24.906
Hello?

113
06:26.407 --> 06:27.283
Sorry?

114
06:28.201 --> 06:29.452
In the trunk of a car?

115
06:30.077 --> 06:31.370
Yes, I'll go.

116
06:32.288 --> 06:33.122
Got it.

117
06:39.253 --> 06:43.508
They found someone who was kidnapped in Seoul and escaped in Gunsan.

118
06:45.593 --> 06:47.303
Remember what that Chinese man said?

119
06:49.764 --> 06:52.141
The victim also saw a tiger at the kidnapper's house.

120
07:46.988 --> 07:49.156
THE BLUE ROAD

121
07:51.242 --> 07:54.328
HANBIT HOSPITAL

122
07:54.412 --> 07:57.748
The victim's testimony matches a case we're investigating.

123
07:58.749 --> 08:01.502
How did she manage to escape while anesthetized?

124
08:02.128 --> 08:06.215
Ms. Lee Hyeon-seo had a tracheostomy due to a childhood laryngeal tumor.

125
08:06.299 --> 08:09.927
Because of that, she has been taking narcotic painkillers all her life.

126
08:10.428 --> 08:12.597
The silver lining is that due to her tracheostomy,

127
08:12.680 --> 08:14.223
when she was kidnapped,

128
08:15.266 --> 08:17.435
the anesthetic didn't knock her out completely.

129
08:17.935 --> 08:19.729
So that's how she was able to escape?

130
08:20.229 --> 08:21.063
Yes.

131
08:22.189 --> 08:24.358
But that's also why she turned to drugs.

132
08:26.652 --> 08:29.947
The patient has congenital heart problems, so she's vulnerable to shock.

133
08:30.531 --> 08:32.325
Please be careful not to distress her.

134
08:38.372 --> 08:42.835
Once again, the culprit used Speed K as bait to lure their victim.

135
08:44.795 --> 08:46.172
Well, let's meet her.

136
08:53.220 --> 08:54.221
Excuse me.

137
08:54.305 --> 08:57.433
We're from the Seoul Metropolitan Police. We'd like to speak with…

138
09:11.614 --> 09:12.657
That bastard…

139
09:14.241 --> 09:16.118
I want him caught.

140
09:18.621 --> 09:20.873
But I didn't get a good look at his face.

141
09:25.711 --> 09:27.713
I really want him caught, though.

142
09:45.231 --> 09:46.190
We can

143
09:47.066 --> 09:48.317
catch the guy.

144
09:50.986 --> 09:53.531
But we need your help.

145
09:55.366 --> 09:56.534
It might be

146
09:57.034 --> 09:58.369
a little hard for you.

147
10:01.580 --> 10:03.541
Inose, what are you talking about?

148
10:05.876 --> 10:08.295
Yes, it's a method the FBI guys also use

149
10:08.796 --> 10:11.799
during the early stages of their investigations.

150
10:11.882 --> 10:12.717
And Inose says

151
10:13.509 --> 10:15.136
he's done it before,

152
10:15.219 --> 10:17.847
both during his training in the States and in the field…

153
10:17.930 --> 10:20.391
I heard she's from an orphanage and has no guardian.

154
10:21.142 --> 10:24.186
Are you going to take responsibility? Are you?

155
10:24.270 --> 10:26.897
Chief Gu messed up once. I should get a chance too.

156
10:28.274 --> 10:29.734
I'll take responsibility.

157
10:31.277 --> 10:32.111
Hey.

158
10:39.994 --> 10:42.997
Let's give it a shot. We have to try everything we can.

159
10:53.632 --> 10:56.719
My daughter liked this.

160
11:16.781 --> 11:18.783
Here. Take it.

161
11:33.047 --> 11:34.799
Buy yourself an ice cream.

162
11:40.638 --> 11:42.389
Now, relax.

163
11:56.987 --> 11:59.907
I'm going to count to ten.

164
12:01.742 --> 12:02.785
One.

165
12:03.536 --> 12:04.370
Two.

166
12:05.830 --> 12:06.705
Three.

167
12:08.457 --> 12:09.333
Four.

168
12:11.168 --> 12:12.545
Five.

169
12:14.171 --> 12:15.256
Six.

170
12:17.216 --> 12:18.342
Seven.

171
12:20.427 --> 12:21.637
Eight.

172
12:27.852 --> 12:29.478
It's dark.

173
12:32.940 --> 12:34.358
Pitch dark.

174
12:37.236 --> 12:40.239
I can hear someone playing the piano.

175
12:43.450 --> 12:44.827
An old house.

176
12:47.913 --> 12:51.667
It looks like an old house.

177
12:55.546 --> 12:57.381
There's a tiger.

178
13:02.344 --> 13:04.555
It's a tiger-shaped…

179
13:11.478 --> 13:12.563
device.

180
13:18.444 --> 13:20.237
He's coming closer.

181
13:27.578 --> 13:29.288
I pretended to be asleep.

182
13:34.835 --> 13:36.128
And then,

183
13:37.004 --> 13:38.505
when he let his guard down…

184
14:11.163 --> 14:12.414
I'm scared.

185
14:15.834 --> 14:17.127
But…

186
14:19.546 --> 14:21.090
he must be caught.

187
14:25.177 --> 14:26.720
Please catch him.

188
14:29.890 --> 14:32.685
If you don't, I feel like he'll come find me again.

189
14:33.477 --> 14:35.145
Please catch him.

190
14:36.647 --> 14:37.815
We will.

191
14:40.359 --> 14:44.613
WELCOME TO GUNSAN

192
14:44.697 --> 14:47.282
The culprit kidnapped the victim in Seoul,

193
14:47.366 --> 14:50.327
loaded her into a large vehicle, and transported her to Gunsan!

194
14:50.828 --> 14:54.456
Look for old houses and cars that could have been modified!

195
14:54.540 --> 14:57.960
And check every Japanese person living in Gunsan. Got it?

196
14:58.043 --> 14:58.877
Yes, sir!

197
14:58.961 --> 15:00.087
It's so cramped in here.

198
15:00.170 --> 15:01.755
Move it! We don't have forever.

199
15:01.839 --> 15:02.881
Yes, sir.

200
15:02.965 --> 15:04.967
I told you not to put this up here!

201
15:05.050 --> 15:07.344
-How many times did I tell you? -Get a move on!

202
15:07.886 --> 15:08.929
-Understood. -So…

203
15:09.763 --> 15:12.933
This is the operations base?

204
15:13.017 --> 15:14.643
This is the Korean way for you.

205
15:15.144 --> 15:16.145
Right.

206
15:17.521 --> 15:20.816
Inspector Kim, what's Mr. Hypnotist saying?

207
15:21.692 --> 15:23.318
Right, well…

208
15:25.320 --> 15:27.448
He said that Korea is

209
15:27.948 --> 15:31.035
good at these large-scale undercover investigations.

210
15:32.870 --> 15:33.871
We're awesome, yeah?

211
15:35.581 --> 15:38.542
He looks like he bites, but I see he's actually a cutie.

212
15:38.625 --> 15:41.837
We really can't fuck up this time! Got it?

213
15:41.920 --> 15:43.213
Yes, sir!

214
15:43.297 --> 15:44.465
This is an undercover op.

215
15:44.548 --> 15:46.842
-The Gunsan police can't know. -Yes, sir!

216
15:48.343 --> 15:49.845
This is the operations base.

217
15:50.345 --> 15:51.180
What?

218
15:54.600 --> 15:56.935
As you probably noticed on the way,

219
15:57.436 --> 15:59.146
Gunsan is a pretty small city.

220
16:01.565 --> 16:03.192
He'll know right away.

221
16:03.692 --> 16:04.651
Know what?

222
16:07.696 --> 16:12.409
That we've set up a special investigation HQ and are closing in.

223
16:12.493 --> 16:13.660
The culprit, I mean.

224
16:17.539 --> 16:20.292
After Lee Hyeon-seo escaped, she ran for around an hour.

225
16:20.375 --> 16:23.128
That puts a five-kilometer radius around where she was found.

226
16:23.754 --> 16:27.299
A place with enough space to park a large vehicle

227
16:28.759 --> 16:30.427
and that also has a large basement.

228
16:30.511 --> 16:32.387
That's what we're looking for.

229
16:32.471 --> 16:36.600
Well, that's something that Chief Gu and the boys can handle.

230
16:40.437 --> 16:43.524
As for us, shall we use our brains to find him?

231
16:45.984 --> 16:48.737
What the Chinese man and Lee Hyeon-seo mentioned…

232
16:49.655 --> 16:50.989
This tiger device.

233
16:54.076 --> 16:56.578
A device shaped like a tiger…

234
16:58.831 --> 17:01.125
Could it be some sort of torture device?

235
17:04.670 --> 17:06.463
This obviously isn't it.

236
17:09.633 --> 17:11.552
Right. A device like this

237
17:12.344 --> 17:15.305
would crush the bones completely, not just twist the joints.

238
17:16.598 --> 17:19.309
So if you tie down the hands and feet, then turn the handle,

239
17:19.393 --> 17:23.021
the whole body gets pulled apart and just goes "crack"?

240
17:24.439 --> 17:25.482
Crack.

241
17:26.108 --> 17:28.152
Crack.

242
17:33.866 --> 17:35.033
The sound

243
17:36.577 --> 17:37.953
of bones breaking.

244
17:40.539 --> 17:41.665
The sound?

245
17:45.294 --> 17:47.754
What if it isn't a torture device?

246
17:51.967 --> 17:54.595
The sound of bones breaking, the sound of screams…

247
17:56.430 --> 17:59.349
And the sound of the piano Lee Hyeon-seo heard.

248
18:04.438 --> 18:06.773
He's obsessed with sounds?

249
18:10.068 --> 18:11.904
What if it isn't torture at all?

250
18:14.072 --> 18:15.490
It isn't torture?

251
18:17.284 --> 18:18.535
The piano.

252
18:19.661 --> 18:21.371
He plays people like instruments?

253
18:22.372 --> 18:23.207
Yes.

254
18:27.252 --> 18:29.796
LARGE TIGER MUSICAL INSTRUMENT

255
18:34.343 --> 18:35.594
You see this, right?

256
18:37.137 --> 18:38.805
The Tiger of the Ancestral Mountain.

257
18:42.517 --> 18:44.228
THE TIGER OF THE ANCESTRAL MOUNTAIN

258
18:44.311 --> 18:48.398
"This tiger symbolizes the Joseon tiger during the Japanese colonial era."

259
18:48.482 --> 18:50.567
"This art piece turns the great tiger

260
18:50.651 --> 18:53.862
that once terrorized the Korean Peninsula into a musical instrument."

261
18:55.280 --> 18:57.282
"When activated, it is said to play the sound

262
18:57.366 --> 18:59.284
of bones breaking and muscles snapping."

263
18:59.368 --> 19:01.870
"However, its method of operation is unknown."

264
19:05.958 --> 19:07.960
EMI SHUNSUKE CREATING AND PERFORMING BEAUTY

265
19:11.338 --> 19:12.714
"E-M-I"…

266
19:13.215 --> 19:14.883
It definitely said "Emi"…

267
19:15.425 --> 19:16.927
No, "E-M-I"!

268
19:18.595 --> 19:19.763
"Emi Shunsuke."

269
19:20.555 --> 19:21.515
A Japanese?

270
19:25.018 --> 19:26.311
GUNSAN FOREIGN RESIDENT REGISTRY

271
19:26.395 --> 19:27.479
Emi…

272
19:28.230 --> 19:30.107
Is this like his pseudonym?

273
19:30.190 --> 19:31.900
Emi Shunsuke.

274
19:31.984 --> 19:32.943
Emi…

275
19:33.443 --> 19:36.613
Emi Shunsuke, resides in a detached house at 35-47 Buksan-dong.

276
19:37.364 --> 19:38.573
Buksan-dong.

277
19:39.157 --> 19:41.201
Within a five-kilometer radius of where Lee was found?

278
19:41.285 --> 19:42.244
Yes.

279
19:50.669 --> 19:54.089
Chief, it's urgent, so I'm leaving a voicemail. Please call me back.

280
19:54.172 --> 19:55.215
Detective Kim.

281
19:55.882 --> 19:59.177
Emi from Emi Shunsuke and Emi as in General Emiri sound the same.

282
19:59.261 --> 20:01.388
Emi is a rare surname, even in Japan.

283
20:02.639 --> 20:04.725
And if I don't answer your call later,

284
20:06.184 --> 20:07.936
please track my location.

285
20:29.958 --> 20:31.668
Has he already taken off?

286
20:39.885 --> 20:41.345
I've seen this somewhere before.

287
20:45.015 --> 20:46.224
Don't.

288
20:48.310 --> 20:49.269
That.

289
20:53.023 --> 20:58.070
What kind of assholes would even think to park a bus here?

290
20:58.153 --> 21:00.572
It needs to be towed away to teach them a lesson.

291
21:01.239 --> 21:03.200
Is this your bus? Move it now. Right now.

292
21:03.283 --> 21:04.576
I'm from the Seoul police.

293
21:05.744 --> 21:07.245
-Police? -Yes.

294
21:07.329 --> 21:09.956
Do you know a man named Emi Shunsuke who lives here?

295
21:12.793 --> 21:15.545
-Shunsuke is the artist who lives here. -An artist?

296
21:15.629 --> 21:17.005
-Yes. -Where is he right now?

297
21:17.089 --> 21:18.590
Hello.

298
21:18.673 --> 21:20.842
I'm Inose Hiroshi.

299
21:20.926 --> 21:22.511
I'm from Japan.

300
21:24.721 --> 21:26.348
-You're Japanese? -Yes.

301
21:27.933 --> 21:29.393
Emi Shunsuke…

302
21:29.476 --> 21:32.062
I'm a friend of Shunsuke's from his hometown.

303
21:32.145 --> 21:34.439
-You're a friend from home? -Yes.

304
21:34.523 --> 21:38.026
I came to see an old friend I lost touch with long ago,

305
21:38.527 --> 21:41.029
and the Korean police are helping me.

306
21:43.115 --> 21:44.950
-Is that right? -Yes.

307
21:47.035 --> 21:48.912
You've sure come a long way in this heat.

308
21:49.830 --> 21:50.664
I see.

309
21:56.628 --> 21:57.546
Why?

310
21:59.756 --> 22:00.632
What?

311
22:03.802 --> 22:07.180
You came all this way to meet your friend, but I have nothing to offer you.

312
22:08.014 --> 22:09.307
I feel so bad.

313
22:09.975 --> 22:11.810
-Please have some of this. -Thank you.

314
22:11.893 --> 22:13.437
Yes, have some watermelon.

315
22:14.062 --> 22:15.439
You two must be close.

316
22:16.106 --> 22:18.650
Well, when it comes to Mr. Emi,

317
22:18.733 --> 22:23.113
he's always so mild-mannered and soft-spoken.

318
22:23.780 --> 22:27.075
And when he's away from home on one of his longer business trips,

319
22:27.159 --> 22:29.619
I hold onto his deliveries for him and such…

320
22:29.703 --> 22:31.079
Is he away from home often?

321
22:33.457 --> 22:35.292
Well, occasionally.

322
22:35.792 --> 22:39.337
Since he puts on performances and exhibitions and all that.

323
22:39.421 --> 22:41.214
Here. Drink some of this while we talk.

324
22:46.678 --> 22:48.680
Has Shunsuke…

325
22:50.348 --> 22:52.350
lived here long?

326
22:52.434 --> 22:54.186
I'm not sure.

327
22:54.686 --> 22:57.606
He's been living in that house since before I moved here,

328
22:57.689 --> 22:59.816
so he must have been here for quite some time.

329
22:59.900 --> 23:01.985
He's quite well-known in the neighborhood too.

330
23:02.068 --> 23:04.571
He does a lot of volunteer work around here.

331
23:05.864 --> 23:10.118
Actually, I think I heard the house has been in his family for generations.

332
23:10.202 --> 23:11.036
Generations.

333
23:13.288 --> 23:17.334
As you can see for yourselves, the house is quiet.

334
23:17.417 --> 23:20.962
He says it's perfect for him to work undisturbed.

335
23:22.047 --> 23:23.798
In my humble opinion,

336
23:24.382 --> 23:26.343
I guess that's the thing with art.

337
23:26.426 --> 23:30.555
You need a place like that to get those sparks of inspiration.

338
23:30.639 --> 23:33.266
I became a fan myself after living next door to him.

339
23:35.685 --> 23:39.272
Talk about a bad time to get a call. Who is it?

340
23:42.108 --> 23:43.193
Hello?

341
23:43.735 --> 23:45.028
Mr. Emi.

342
23:46.530 --> 23:48.156
Did the rehearsal go well?

343
23:50.450 --> 23:53.703
Two days? Don't even worry about it.

344
23:53.787 --> 23:56.331
I'm now a pro at garden care.

345
24:00.460 --> 24:01.795
How did you know?

346
24:03.213 --> 24:04.130
Okay.

347
24:05.966 --> 24:07.259
He wants to talk.

348
24:10.053 --> 24:11.054
Sorry?

349
24:11.137 --> 24:13.640
Come on, Mr. Emi is waiting.

350
24:14.349 --> 24:16.518
-Me? -Yes. Hurry up and take it.

351
24:17.102 --> 24:19.104
Goodness, don't keep him waiting.

352
24:22.774 --> 24:24.150
Yes, hello?

353
24:24.234 --> 24:25.902
You're a detective, correct?

354
24:30.156 --> 24:32.534
I don't know why you're looking for me,

355
24:34.452 --> 24:37.372
and my Korean's still a bit rough, but…

356
24:38.748 --> 24:41.167
Am I the culprit?

357
24:42.043 --> 24:43.461
Could I be the culprit?

358
24:50.552 --> 24:52.762
I'm at the police station now.

359
25:06.484 --> 25:08.320
-This man here… -Enjoy.

360
25:08.403 --> 25:10.864
He bought us buns to thank us for our hard work.

361
25:10.947 --> 25:12.824
You know he's a famous artist, right?

362
25:12.907 --> 25:14.367
Can I help you?

363
25:14.451 --> 25:15.785
Say "thank you," punks.

364
25:15.869 --> 25:16.911
Please enjoy.

365
25:17.746 --> 25:18.788
Keep up the good work.

366
25:19.664 --> 25:20.707
Enjoy.

367
25:23.001 --> 25:25.962
Anyone who hasn't grabbed a bun, come grab one.

368
25:32.886 --> 25:34.012
Hello.

369
25:41.603 --> 25:43.396
There's only one left…

370
25:53.406 --> 25:54.949
Nice to meet you.

371
26:04.167 --> 26:06.002
I'm Emi Shunsuke.

372
26:08.171 --> 26:11.174
Why do you look disappointed?

373
26:20.725 --> 26:21.976
Hey, what gives?

374
26:23.269 --> 26:25.063
-What's happening here? -What the…

375
26:26.898 --> 26:28.483
What? An undercover investigation?

376
26:30.193 --> 26:31.111
Holy smokes.

377
26:31.778 --> 26:34.447
Those wretched sons of guns.

378
26:34.948 --> 26:38.034
They've practically set up a cozy little home here, eh?

379
26:38.118 --> 26:41.705
They've got themselves a secret base here. What is all this?

380
26:41.788 --> 26:44.040
This is a complete trainwreck. What should we do?

381
26:47.335 --> 26:48.670
Kim Seok, that bastard.

382
26:48.753 --> 26:52.799
What, you think Gunsan is such a joke that we weren't even worth looping in?

383
26:52.882 --> 26:54.551
Why would you put it that way?

384
26:54.634 --> 26:56.886
We just had to keep the investigation tight!

385
26:56.970 --> 27:00.014
All right, that's enough. Here's the official paperwork.

386
27:00.098 --> 27:02.976
Give us a fucking break. This is our jurisdiction!

387
27:03.059 --> 27:04.936
You think official paperwork is a joke?

388
27:08.148 --> 27:09.441
INTERROGATION ROOM

389
27:09.524 --> 27:12.444
Okay, fine! But if you don't get anything out of him, I swear--

390
27:13.111 --> 27:14.988
What you said over the phone earlier…

391
27:15.488 --> 27:17.240
What was it I said?

392
27:26.207 --> 27:27.959
Hey.

393
27:30.128 --> 27:31.629
You know,

394
27:33.339 --> 27:36.301
you're quite young for a famous artist.

395
27:37.594 --> 27:38.845
Am I?

396
27:42.265 --> 27:43.975
Isn't it a little funny?

397
27:44.058 --> 27:47.479
Two Japanese people, sitting in a Korean police station.

398
27:47.562 --> 27:48.813
Not at all.

399
27:49.314 --> 27:51.900
I'm only interrogating you because I speak Japanese.

400
27:52.525 --> 27:55.487
Exhibition planning, pianist, sound art performance…

401
27:55.570 --> 27:57.697
What kind of work is this, exactly?

402
27:59.157 --> 28:01.534
Why, it's art, of course.

403
28:01.618 --> 28:03.328
For the eyes and ears.

404
28:03.411 --> 28:06.372
I create works that are multisensory.

405
28:07.248 --> 28:09.793
If you'd like, you could come to my upcoming show.

406
28:09.876 --> 28:13.713
This time, it'll be an interactive sound art performance--

407
28:13.797 --> 28:16.841
You made The Tiger of the Ancestral Mountain, didn't you?

408
28:18.218 --> 28:21.513
It says here you travel between Korea and Japan for work.

409
28:21.596 --> 28:23.181
Does the tiger come with you?

410
28:23.264 --> 28:26.726
The tiger's both an exhibit and music.

411
28:26.810 --> 28:30.146
It's a one-of-a-kind artwork that has no singular definition.

412
28:30.230 --> 28:33.107
The sounds, the process of creating those sounds are beautiful--

413
28:33.191 --> 28:34.484
Just like…

414
28:38.112 --> 28:39.948
murder, you mean?

415
28:53.837 --> 28:55.880
Your voice, Mr. Inose…

416
28:57.966 --> 29:00.176
It has a wonderful energy.

417
29:00.760 --> 29:02.053
So what if it does?

418
29:02.554 --> 29:06.558
It may be a little higher than the average man's voice,

419
29:06.641 --> 29:09.227
but strong energy creates soundwaves

420
29:09.727 --> 29:12.856
that stimulate the frequencies flowing through our minds and bodies.

421
29:13.523 --> 29:16.067
I never went to college. Stop speaking in riddles.

422
29:16.776 --> 29:19.153
Such a soothing voice.

423
29:19.237 --> 29:22.156
The kind that inspires the human soul.

424
29:22.657 --> 29:24.951
The kind that makes you want to play it.

425
29:30.540 --> 29:33.751
You're sure highbrow for a murderer.

426
29:38.965 --> 29:40.717
What time is it now?

427
29:54.564 --> 29:57.108
He had the nerve to bring the vehicle to the station?

428
29:57.191 --> 29:59.193
Hey. Don't touch that, okay?

429
30:00.445 --> 30:03.489
-I swear, if there's a single hair… -How long must we wait?

430
30:03.990 --> 30:05.408
Can't we just jimmy this open?

431
30:05.491 --> 30:06.326
Hey.

432
30:06.826 --> 30:08.494
We need a warrant first.

433
30:08.578 --> 30:10.914
-Just wait. -Oh, for crying out loud!

434
30:10.997 --> 30:12.832
Well, would you look at that.

435
30:12.916 --> 30:15.752
What are you people, neighborhood thugs?

436
30:15.835 --> 30:17.629
-What's with the tools? -What?

437
30:17.712 --> 30:19.631
-Why don't you just smash it? -Easy.

438
30:19.714 --> 30:21.257
You came here to pull this shit?

439
30:21.341 --> 30:25.595
You can't touch that until the suspect talks.

440
30:28.848 --> 30:29.849
Yum.

441
30:38.316 --> 30:39.692
You're not going to eat?

442
30:40.443 --> 30:43.029
The vehicle you drove here's pretty big.

443
30:43.112 --> 30:45.907
The equipment I use and my artworks are huge, you see.

444
30:45.990 --> 30:50.328
Right. Perfect for hauling equipment and for kidnapping people.

445
30:51.704 --> 30:53.456
And you have to load the tiger too.

446
30:53.539 --> 30:56.501
How many people fit in that trunk?

447
30:58.086 --> 31:01.839
If they're corpses, I suppose you could fit more than if they were alive.

448
31:02.382 --> 31:04.634
Especially if their limbs were broken.

449
31:06.678 --> 31:08.096
Who knows?

450
31:08.680 --> 31:10.682
I've never put a person in the trunk before.

451
31:11.182 --> 31:13.434
I don't have a family, and I live alone, you see.

452
31:14.477 --> 31:18.481
I heard that house was inherited, but your parents' names

453
31:18.982 --> 31:21.651
weren't in any records or family registers.

454
31:23.403 --> 31:26.823
Did your rich parents remove you from the family register?

455
31:28.366 --> 31:30.326
Do your parents know?

456
31:31.244 --> 31:33.079
That their son is a murderer?

457
31:36.290 --> 31:39.669
Do I really have to divulge such personal details?

458
31:41.045 --> 31:42.088
Yes.

459
31:44.173 --> 31:45.800
You do.

460
31:46.718 --> 31:47.593
Oh, look.

461
31:48.094 --> 31:50.263
Your chair's crooked.

462
31:57.645 --> 31:59.981
Did you try to kill your family too?

463
32:00.064 --> 32:01.315
Or

464
32:01.983 --> 32:03.818
did they witness your crime?

465
32:04.569 --> 32:07.655
Detective, you have quite the imagination.

466
32:08.364 --> 32:09.240
What…

467
32:11.075 --> 32:12.368
Detective.

468
32:13.536 --> 32:14.370
Yes?

469
32:15.913 --> 32:16.914
Tell me.

470
32:17.749 --> 32:19.000
What…

471
32:22.462 --> 32:23.796
time is it now?

472
32:29.969 --> 32:32.472
That really hurt.

473
32:37.268 --> 32:39.020
He was in Jeju Island when Park In-gyu died.

474
32:39.103 --> 32:40.354
No drug-related priors.

475
32:40.438 --> 32:42.565
No flight records around Miyashita Aki's murder.

476
32:42.648 --> 32:43.608
It's all doctored.

477
32:44.192 --> 32:46.319
So we won't be getting a search warrant?

478
32:46.402 --> 32:47.653
No.

479
32:48.196 --> 32:49.238
A confession.

480
32:50.156 --> 32:52.617
We just need to get a confession. We still have time.

481
32:53.242 --> 32:54.660
That bastard is the culprit.

482
32:55.495 --> 32:56.746
Do you remember?

483
32:58.873 --> 33:01.626
Emi asked that woman to look after his garden for two days.

484
33:02.752 --> 33:06.005
Without a warrant, we can only arrest and detain him for up to 48 hours.

485
33:07.090 --> 33:10.259
What happens in Korea if he gets released after 48 hours

486
33:10.343 --> 33:11.969
because no evidence was found?

487
33:21.771 --> 33:23.523
Without new evidence, we can't…

488
33:27.902 --> 33:29.695
get a warrant for the same charge.

489
33:30.279 --> 33:31.405
In other words…

490
33:32.448 --> 33:35.118
He won't confess.

491
33:44.752 --> 33:46.420
Incident confirmed.

492
33:46.921 --> 33:49.173
Team 2, move out.

493
33:55.346 --> 33:56.597
-Excuse me. -Hey!

494
33:56.681 --> 33:57.765
What's going on here?

495
33:58.850 --> 34:01.018
Another body was found.

496
34:01.102 --> 34:02.520
We're totally fucked.

497
34:02.603 --> 34:04.188
Chief, hurry!

498
36:04.267 --> 36:05.476
What are you doing?

499
36:06.060 --> 36:06.894
What are you…

500
36:08.479 --> 36:09.438
Oh, boy!

501
36:11.274 --> 36:12.984
Goksan Elementary School staff, Yoo I-jin.

502
36:13.067 --> 36:15.236
Sorry? Please speak in Japanese.

503
36:15.319 --> 36:16.529
Another murder already?

504
36:17.029 --> 36:18.656
Stop! That's enough!

505
36:18.739 --> 36:19.573
Let go!

506
36:19.657 --> 36:20.658
I said, enough!

507
36:21.617 --> 36:22.451
Kim Seok!

508
36:23.452 --> 36:26.289
Calm down! You're a cop!

509
36:33.421 --> 36:34.880
Kim Seok.

510
36:39.302 --> 36:40.845
Thank you for your hard work,

511
36:42.305 --> 36:44.432
Detective Kim Seok.

512
36:50.187 --> 36:53.399
While the suspect was subject to intense questioning for over 40 hours

513
36:53.482 --> 36:56.444
for owning a vehicle and house that fit the profile,

514
36:56.527 --> 36:59.572
the victim may have been desperately waiting to be rescued.

515
37:00.156 --> 37:03.159
Amid concerns that this could spark diplomatic tensions with Japan

516
37:03.242 --> 37:05.411
and put a damper on the Korea-Japan World Cup--

517
37:05.494 --> 37:06.787
It's Emi Shunsuke!

518
37:08.456 --> 37:11.584
Stop the reporters! Keep them back!

519
37:13.294 --> 37:14.795
How are you feeling right now?

520
37:15.379 --> 37:18.341
Is it true you were subjected to coercive questioning for two days?

521
37:18.424 --> 37:20.176
Have you spoken with your family?

522
37:20.259 --> 37:22.970
-I said, stay back! -Did they disregard you from the start?

523
37:23.054 --> 37:25.723
Was there no use of coercion? Please say a few words!

524
37:25.806 --> 37:27.058
Quiet!

525
37:40.738 --> 37:42.031
What… Get this on camera!

526
37:42.114 --> 37:43.532
-Record this. -Okay.

527
37:45.701 --> 37:46.911
I…

528
37:49.121 --> 37:50.539
didn't do anything!

529
37:51.832 --> 37:53.626
Please, search all you want.

530
38:03.010 --> 38:05.096
Follow him.

531
38:11.185 --> 38:14.814
Even with a search warrant, we'd have found nothing in that car.

532
38:15.981 --> 38:19.693
After dumping the body, he deliberately turned up at the police station.

533
38:20.236 --> 38:22.655
That must be why he asked for the time earlier.

534
38:22.738 --> 38:25.991
He was probably calculating the time it would take

535
38:26.534 --> 38:29.412
for a warehouse worker to show up to work and call it in.

536
38:32.873 --> 38:34.083
What if…

537
38:37.461 --> 38:40.714
If I'd tracked Emi Shunsuke's movements first

538
38:41.215 --> 38:43.592
instead of placing him under emergency arrest…

539
38:44.969 --> 38:47.346
Better yet, if I had searched the surrounding area…

540
38:52.101 --> 38:53.936
could I have saved the victim?

541
38:55.813 --> 38:58.524
The crime scene was over 30 kilometers from here.

542
38:58.607 --> 39:00.443
We searched the entire five-kilometer radius.

543
39:00.526 --> 39:01.944
We couldn't have predicted--

544
39:02.027 --> 39:03.821
That's why I said "what if."

545
39:07.908 --> 39:08.993
Cops

546
39:09.785 --> 39:10.786
don't deal

547
39:11.287 --> 39:12.371
in what-ifs.

548
39:22.882 --> 39:25.968
HE'S FILING A COMPLAINT LATER TODAY GET HERE NOW! FROM: HEAD OF UNIT

549
39:26.051 --> 39:28.971
He's filing an official complaint with the Seoul Police.

550
39:31.432 --> 39:32.433
Bastard.

551
39:33.225 --> 39:35.144
Lucky for us, I guess.

552
39:35.227 --> 39:36.103
What?

553
39:37.605 --> 39:41.984
That means his house will be empty, doesn't it?

554
39:46.447 --> 39:48.491
I'll go.

555
39:49.492 --> 39:50.743
Alone? In Korea?

556
39:50.826 --> 39:52.453
-Yes. -No.

557
39:53.162 --> 39:54.413
It's dangerous.

558
39:56.332 --> 39:58.125
We told her we'd catch him, didn't we?

559
40:00.753 --> 40:02.004
Lee Hyeon-seo…

560
40:03.631 --> 40:04.590
asked us

561
40:05.591 --> 40:06.800
to catch him.

562
40:12.223 --> 40:14.850
It's fine. I'm here on assignment anyway.

563
40:19.563 --> 40:20.814
Please be careful.

564
40:53.806 --> 40:55.808
This'll be a breeze.

565
40:58.394 --> 41:00.187
It's been a while.

566
41:10.573 --> 41:13.075
Yeah, I'm fine.

567
41:18.414 --> 41:21.417
This doesn't look like Korea. It's straight-up Japan.

568
47:09.056 --> 47:13.310
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
